1. 📧 Email Prompt Template

Write an email with the following details:

Purpose: [reason for writing the email]
Recipient: [teacher/manager/company/friend/etc.]
Tone: [formal/professional/friendly/polite]
Key points to include:
- [Point 1]
- [Point 2]
- [Point 3]

Length: [short/medium/detailed]
Include:
- Appropriate subject line
- Professional greeting
- Clear and concise body
- Polite closing
- Call to action, if required

Make the email grammatically correct and professional.

2. 📝 Essay Prompt Template
Act as an expert essay writer.

Write an essay on the topic: [TOPIC]

Requirements:
- Target audience: [school/college/general]
- Word count: [500/800/1000 words]
- Tone: [formal/academic/simple]
- Difficulty level: [beginner/intermediate/advanced]

Structure:
1. Introduction
2. Main body with [number] paragraphs
3. Examples/facts where appropriate
4. Conclusion

Use simple and clear language.
Make the essay original, well-organized, and grammatically correct.

3. 📰 Blog Prompt Template
Act as a professional blogger and content writer.

Write an engaging blog post on: [TOPIC]

Target audience: [AUDIENCE]
Purpose: [educate/inform/entertain/promote]
Tone: [friendly/professional/funny/informative]
Length: [1000 words]

Include:
- Catchy title
- Short introduction/hook
- Clear headings and subheadings
- Practical examples
- Bullet points where useful
- Engaging conclusion
- Call-to-action

Make the blog easy to read, engaging, and SEO-friendly.
Use natural language and avoid unnecessary repetition.
4. ✉️ Letter Prompt Template
Act as an expert letter writer.

Write a [formal/informal] letter about: [PURPOSE/TOPIC]

Sender: [NAME/ROLE]
Recipient: [NAME/ROLE]
Tone: [formal/polite/friendly]
Situation: [DESCRIBE THE SITUATION]

Include:
- Appropriate opening
- Clear explanation of the purpose
- Important details
- Polite request or response
- Appropriate closing

Length: [SHORT/MEDIUM/LONG]

Use grammatically correct and natural language.

5. 📄 Resume Prompt Template
Act as a professional resume writer and career coach.

Create a professional resume for:

Name: [FULL NAME]
Target job/role: [JOB TITLE]
Education: [DEGREE/COLLEGE/YEAR]
Skills: [SKILLS]
Experience: [EXPERIENCE]
Projects: [PROJECTS]
Certifications: [CERTIFICATIONS]
Achievements: [ACHIEVEMENTS]
Languages: [LANGUAGES]

Requirements:
- Keep it ATS-friendly
- Use professional language
- Highlight relevant skills and achievements
- Use strong action verbs
- Keep the format clean and easy to scan
- Do not add fake information
- Keep it to [1/2] pages

Output the resume with clear sections and professional formatting.

6. 📖 Story Prompt Template
Act as a creative fiction writer.

Write an interesting story based on:

Genre: [HORROR/COMEDY/ADVENTURE/SCI-FI/ROMANCE/etc.]
Main character: [CHARACTER]
Setting: [PLACE/TIME]
Main problem/conflict: [CONFLICT]
Theme/message: [MESSAGE]
Ending: [HAPPY/SAD/OPEN/UNEXPECTED]
Length: [SHORT/MEDIUM/LONG]

Requirements:
- Start with an interesting hook
- Develop the characters naturally
- Include dialogue where appropriate
- Build suspense/conflict
- Maintain a clear beginning, middle, and ending
- Make the story original and engaging
- Use vivid but easy-to-understand language
